    "result": "# SOURCE ACCEPT\n\nI reviewed only the supplied diff and unchanged guard/submit source. I did not use tools, make edits or write a plan file. Both visual verdicts stay **NOT VISUALLY VERIFIED**. Full role, native, provider, SQL, device and reference acceptance stays **OPEN**.\n\n## Coverage\nTen files contain twelve owning forms, all guarded:\n\n1. Operator invitation\n2. New legal entity\n3. Legal entity and site record actions (one component; `siteId` picks the action)\n4. New site\n5. Employee onboarding\n6. Department/job create, update, disable and reactivate\n7. Member invite\n8. Bulk ready-attendance approval\n9. Import preview\n10. Import commit\n11. Employment end\n12. Rehire\n\n## Pending state belongs to the right action\n- Every form reads its own `useActionState` third tuple.\n- Import preview uses `previewActionPending` and commit uses `commitActionPending`. Employment end uses `endActionPending` and rehire uses `rehireActionPending`.\n- Bulk approval keeps its existing `pending` for both the button state and the notice.\n- Preview and commit pending stay independent: each `SubmitButton` uses `useFormStatus` scoped to its own form.\n\n## Hook order\n- `useOfflineSubmission` and `useId` run unconditionally at the top of every component.\n- In `NewEmployeeForm`, they run before the setup-gate early return, along with the existing `useActionState` and `useState`. `showOffline0` is computed after the gate, but it is a plain value, not a hook.\n- In `EmploymentLifecyclePanel`, the hooks run before the `canEnd`/`canRehire` render gates.\n\n## Event race\n- `blockOfflineSubmission` reads live `navigator.onLine` inside `onSubmit`, so a click that beats the `offline` event is still stopped.\n- `preventDefault` stops React 19's form-action dispatch, and `refreshSignal` re-syncs the stale snapshot.\n- When the snapshot already says offline, the disabled submit buttons also block implicit (Enter-key) submission.\n- Nothing is dispatched, so React does not reset the form and no `attempt` key changes. Typed fields, the chosen file, selected import rows, selected attendance rows, the acknowledgment checkbox, reasons and date bounds all stay as entered.\n\n## Accessibility IDs and notice\n- Each form instance gets its own `useId`. Components with two forms use separate `offlineHint0` and `offlineHint1`.\n- `RecordActionForm` appears several times per page, and `useId` keeps each instance unique.\n- `aria-describedby` points at the hint only while the notice is rendered, so there are no dangling references.\n- The notice is hidden while that form's own action is pending.\n- It uses `purpose=\"continuation\"`: it asks the user to reconnect to continue and makes no success claim.\n\n## Authority, fields, keys and constraints\n- Hidden inputs and `idempotencyKey` are unchanged in the invitation and member-invite forms.\n- `name=\"intent\"` values, the required acknowledgment, min/max lengths and `required` attributes are unchanged.\n- The existing `ariaLabel`, `danger-button` and `secondary-button` choices are unchanged.\n- Existing error and result rendering is unchanged.\n- Gates are preserved, so forms stay absent where they already were: the setup gate, `canEnd`, `canRehire`, `optionsError`/`!rehireOptions`, `commit.state !== 'imported'` and empty `selectableData`.\n- The org-catalog disable and reactivate buttons get the same `disabled` and `aria-describedby` as the main submit.\n- Search, local reject download, navigation and sign-out are untouched.\n\n## Journey simplicity\n- The online path is identical apart from props that are inert while online.\n- When known offline, the user keeps their inputs and sees one status message beside the blocked action.\n- There is no queue, persistence, automatic resend, global disabling or new abstraction.\n\n## Non-blocking\nThe second `import … from 'react'` line repeats the existing pattern from earlier batches. It only matters if the grouped lint flags duplicate imports.",
